# Always Look Up Current Time

Never guess or fabricate timestamps. Before constructing any time-based query, log window, or tool argument that requires a timestamp, run `date -u` to get the actual current UTC time.

You have no internal clock. The system prompt gives you a date but no time of day. Always anchor to reality first.
